      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "SAPA demonstrates a high level of operational efficiency that exceeds industry standards. Their <cite id=\"7\">81.2% program expense ratio</cite> significantly beats the <cite id=\"13\">75% industry benchmark</cite> and the <cite id=\"14\">82.9% peer median</cite>. This ensures that donor funds are directed almost entirely toward medical supplies and service delivery. Furthermore, the organization maintains <cite id=\"15\">4.3 months of operating reserves</cite>, providing a strong financial cushion for emergency responses in volatile regions like Sudan."
      ],
      "summary": "The Sudanese American Physicians Association (SAPA) is a medical relief organization that builds healthcare systems and provides emergency services in crisis zones. Founded in <cite id=\"1\">2019</cite>, the organization has rapidly scaled its operations to address the humanitarian crisis in Sudan and neighboring Chad. In FY2024, SAPA managed <cite id=\"2\">$7,254,154 in total revenue</cite>, representing significant early-stage growth from its small base of $442,259 in FY2022. The organization maintains a high level of financial accountability, evidenced by a <cite id=\"3\">90/100 overall score from Charity Navigator</cite>. SAPA operates through a direct service model, delivering essential medical care, hunger relief, and water sanitation services. Their efficiency is notable, with a <cite id=\"4\">cost of approximately $6.96 per beneficiary</cite>, which is exceptional for the global health sector. The charity is <cite id=\"5\">zakat-eligible</cite>, specifically serving the poor (fuqara) and needy (masakin). By focusing on both immediate emergency medical care and long-term healthcare infrastructure, SAPA ensures that affected populations have <cite id=\"6\">access to essential healthcare services</cite> during and after conflict.",
